# The 1983 source: FIELD's total past the record is FIELD overflow (DSKCOM.ASM's TEMPB against TEMPA; PC-BASIC lets 15 + 6 into 20); a record past 32767 is Bad record number (DSKRND's JLE: PC-BASIC takes 32768); the FIELD buffer isn't cleared by anything but the bytes written (PC-BASIC's shows zeros where the source's keeps an earlier record's); INPUT # and PRINT # share FD_OPS, and WRITE # pads the record with spaces to two bytes from its end, then CR LF (FIVEO.ASM's WRTFIN, CMPFBC; PC-BASIC doesn't pad)
